# Patch:        010-import-packed-extension-iter
# Phase:        pre
# Target:       multilinear-util/src/eq_batch.rs, multilinear-util/src/poly/maybe_packed.rs, multilinear-util/src/poly/mod.rs, multilinear-util/src/split_eq/eq.rs, multilinear-util/src/split_eq/packed_kernel.rs
# Hunks:        5
# Class:        bound
# Gap:          docs/extractor-issues.md 10 (charon#1266): baby-bear's pre 030
#               moves `to_ext_iter` to the extension trait
#               `PackedFieldExtensionIter` under the cfg. Without this patch
#               p3-multilinear-util does not compile there: E0599,
#               `to_ext_iter` not found, 17 times.
# Cost:         none: every added line is behind cfg(hax_backend_lean), so a
#               normal build is token for token as shipped.
# Upstreamable: no: the imported trait exists only in the extracted variant.
#               Dropping baby-bear's pre 030 makes this patch unnecessary.
# Drop when:    baby-bear's pre 030 is dropped.
# Test:         lint p3-multilinear-util unused_imports
# Mutation:     one import loses its cfg, so a normal build names a trait
#               that does not exist there.
#
# Baby-bear's pre 030 moves `to_ext_iter` onto a blanket extension trait in the extracted variant.
#
# A call resolves only where that trait is in scope, as pre 030 does for p3-matrix.
#
# Each of the five files that calls it imports the trait under the cfg.
#
# In two of them `PackedFieldExtension` was imported only for that call.
#
# Under the cfg that import is unused, so it gets `allow(unused_imports)` there, also only under the cfg.
#
